Drop the raised hover clone when its taskbar item is destroyed

Found on real hardware (NVIDIA RTX, GNOME 50.1): opening an app replaced a
hovered taskbar item, its raised clone survived, and the clone's handlers ran
on the disposed item every frame ("TaskbarItemContainer ... has been already
disposed", three errors per frame at 120 Hz).

--- a/taskbar.js
+++ b/taskbar.js
@@ -1562,6 +1562,12 @@
     _init() {
       super._init()
       this.x_expand = this.y_expand = false
+
+      // An item can be destroyed without animateOutAndDestroy(), e.g. when a
+      // favorite is replaced by its running app while hovered. Drop the raised
+      // clone with it, or the clone's handlers keep using the disposed item and
+      // the clone stays on screen.
+      this.connect('destroy', () => this._raisedClone?.destroy())
     }
 
     vfunc_allocate(box) {
@@ -1739,7 +1745,7 @@
         time: time,
         transition: 'easeOutQuad',
         onComplete: () => {
-          if (!level) {
+          if (!level && this._raisedClone) {
             this._raisedClone.source.opacity = 255
             this._raisedClone.destroy()
             delete this._raisedClone
